FineWine: ray tracing pipelines as one compute shader built on ray queries

Adds VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline.

Metal has no ray generation, hit, miss or callable shader stages, and SPIRV-Cross cannot
translate them; it can translate ray queries. MoltenVKShaderConverter gains a SPIR-V pass
(RayTracingLowering.cpp) that merges the shaders of a pipeline into one compute shader:

- every shader is imported once for each trace depth it can run at, since Metal shaders
  cannot recurse; ids are renumbered, and types, constants and descriptor variables that are
  the same as ones already present are merged;
- the ray tracing storage classes and built-in inputs become private variables;
- OpTraceRayKHR becomes a call to a generated ray query loop that runs any-hit and
  intersection shaders on candidates and then the closest-hit or miss shader, chosen by
  reading the shader binding table through its buffer address;
- OpReportIntersectionKHR and OpExecuteCallableKHR become generated functions; shader records
  are read in place; specialization constants are fixed per stage.

MVKRayTracingPipeline is a compute pipeline made from that shader. vkCmdTraceRaysKHR and
vkCmdTraceRaysIndirectKHR dispatch it with one thread per ray, bind the shader binding
table's addresses, and bind for each traced acceleration structure a texture of its
instances' shader binding table offsets, which a Metal ray query does not return. The ray
tracing bind point keeps its own pipeline and descriptor sets.

Not supported: pipeline libraries, capture/replay handles, arrays of acceleration structures
with non-zero instance offsets.

The new source files are included from existing ones (SPIRVSupport.cpp, MVKPipeline.mm,
MVKCmdDispatch.mm) so that the Xcode projects do not change.

